18:["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"You need Claude Code installed and signed in. Craft Anything runs your own claude program on your own login, so it never sees your account. Then paste this into Claude Code. It finds the right download for your computer, checks it, and runs the doctor before you open the app."}]
29:T46e,Install Craft Anything for me. The only official source is https://github.com/storytold/craft-anything, so don't use any other copy or mirror.

1. Check that Claude Code is installed and signed in (`claude --version`). If it isn't signed in, tell me to run `claude auth login` and stop.
2. Open the latest release on that repo's Releases page and pick the desktop app for my OS and CPU, using the file names listed in the README's Downloads section (the .msi for Windows, the universal .dmg for macOS, the AppImage, .deb or .rpm for Linux). Tell me which file you picked and why before you download it.
3. Check the file against SHA256SUMS.txt from the same release. If the checksum doesn't match, delete it and stop.
4. Install it, then make sure `craft-anything-cli` is on my PATH and run `craft-anything-cli doctor` (if the app didn't put the CLI on my PATH, follow the README). Show me what it reports and fix only what it says is missing, asking me before you install anything else.
5. If there's no desktop build for my system, show me the build-from-source steps in the README (they need Rust 1.97 or newer) and wait for my OK.2a:T46e,Install Craft Anything for me. The only official source is https://github.com/storytold/craft-anything, so don't use any other copy or mirror.

1. Check that Claude Code is installed and signed in (`claude --version`). If it isn't signed in, tell me to run `claude auth login` and stop.
2. Open the latest release on that repo's Releases page and pick the desktop app for my OS and CPU, using the file names listed in the README's Downloads section (the .msi for Windows, the universal .dmg for macOS, the AppImage, .deb or .rpm for Linux). Tell me which file you picked and why before you download it.
3. Check the file against SHA256SUMS.txt from the same release. If the checksum doesn't match, delete it and stop.
4. Install it, then make sure `craft-anything-cli` is on my PATH and run `craft-anything-cli doctor` (if the app didn't put the CLI on my PATH, follow the README). Show me what it reports and fix only what it says is missing, asking me before you install anything else.
5. If there's no desktop build for my system, show me the build-from-source steps in the README (they need Rust 1.97 or newer) and wait for my OK.19:["$","div","6",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"Install Craft Anything"}],["$","$L28",null,{"text":"$29"}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] whitespace-pre-wrap break-words","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"$2a"}]}]]}]
